00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:04.860
And it only matters what race they think I am. Which is, a lot of times, White.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.160
But sometimes, I'll get called in for things that are not my ethnicity.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.160
And that's because of my career.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.880
That's what's important with that.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.720
Three, two, one, go.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.920
Even throughout High School, I just pretended I was White completely.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:33.180
And there was a time when my Dad picked me up from school.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.120
It was a whole thing. People were saying, "Oh, your Dad's a terrorist."

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.640
I had never experienced anything like that

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.640
Or they'd asked me about it and make bomb jokes.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:47.040
It hurt to hear people saying stuff like that about my Dad.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:52.140
Similar thing happened to me. When I was in Elementary School my dad came and dropped me off at school

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.420
And he's a dark-skinned Black man

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.800
And he's from the hood on top of that.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.000
So he has a certain aura to him.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.240
And a lot of people look at me like, That's your dad? And I'm like, yeah, that's my Dad.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.780
And they're like, he looks so scary

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.720
And I'm like, why does he look scary to you? Why should he look scary to you?

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.360
And the only thing that's keeping me away from this "Strongly Disagree"

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:15.980
Is because when I was younger, I just did not accept the Black part of myself. And now, I do.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.500
I just want to say, "I'm really sorry," to both of you.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:21.220
That you felt like you've been put in positions to feel

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:23.580
That is such a terrible thing to tell someone.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.880
No, you can't be every part of who you are.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:30.440
These past couple of years, I've been trying to reconnect with that part

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:34.700
Because I shoved it down for so long and it's been really heart-breaking

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.440
The amount of Wudus I missed and the Ramadans I didn't celebrate

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.540
Because I felt so uncomfortable about that.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.220
It's important to take the steps though.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.740
Personally, I've never tried to hide any part of me.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.440
That's always been the biggest thing for me.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.560
Growing up, I was always proud to be White and I was always proud to be Black.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.900
That's just how I was raised.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:57.480
It's always how it was. I just wanted to be me. So, that's what it is.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:02.260
The reason I'm on this line is because Western beauty standards suck.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.880
They really, really got to me.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:09.280
I would be really picky about how I would do my hair. And how I would part my hair.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.240
And then when I would post YouTube videos or Instagram posts

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.460
I would color-correct everything to be really blue so that I wouldn't look "yellow."

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.620
And it was just, like I didn't want to post a photo of me outside

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.860
Because I thought my eyes looked too Asian.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:30.120
A lot of internalized things that made me feel... made me hate myself and my appearance.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:37.420
And now I feel much more accepting of being mixed and being everything that I am.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:43.640
But I am here because I have felt like I wanted to hide a part of me.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.620
Because it would have been easier for me.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.780
I agree.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:52.900
Like, when I was younger. I used to want to be lighter. I used to get made fun of.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.840
I would always get the question, "Are you adopted?"

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:59.280
You're not Asian. And it just made me feel so bad about myself.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:04.720
That I was so confused. I didn't fit into any single pocket of anybody and any friend groups.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:07.080
I couldn't hang out with the Chinese kids because

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.580
They're like, "You don't look Chinese."

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.060
I don't hang out with the Black kids because I don't sound Black and they say I am White-washed.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:16.400
So my whole entire life, I've literally battled within. Like, what the hell am I?

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.760
Three, two, one, go.

